# Copy this file to .env in the project root (not install/) and adjust
# values. See conf/config.py for the full list of supported variables and
# their defaults.

YCPLT_HOST=0.0.0.0
YCPLT_PORT=4011

# ============================================================================
# RECOMMENDED MODEL PAIR — read this whole block before touching MODEL=/
# INPAINT_MODEL= below. This is TWO SEPARATE FILES from the same repo, one
# for each of two DIFFERENT settings — a real, reported source of confusion:
# downloading only one of them (usually just the one whose wget command sits
# next to whichever setting you're editing) still "works" with no error, it
# just means MODEL and INPAINT_MODEL end up pointing at mismatched or
# nonexistent files. Download BOTH now if you want this recommendation at
# all, then set BOTH MODEL= and INPAINT_MODEL= below to match:
#
#   wget -O models/Realistic_Vision_V6.0_NV_B1_fp16.safetensors \
#     "https://huggingface.co/SG161222/Realistic_Vision_V6.0_B1_noVAE/resolve/main/Realistic_Vision_V6.0_NV_B1_fp16.safetensors"
#   wget -O models/Realistic_Vision_V6.0_NV_B1_inpainting_fp16.safetensors \
#     "https://huggingface.co/SG161222/Realistic_Vision_V6.0_B1_noVAE/resolve/main/Realistic_Vision_V6.0_NV_B1_inpainting_fp16.safetensors"
#
# File 1 (no "_inpainting" in the name) -> MODEL=       (txt2img/img2img)
# File 2 (has "_inpainting" in the name) -> INPAINT_MODEL=  (masked edits,
#                                            including "remove X" jobs)
#
# THIRD required download — do not skip this one. Both files above are
# "noVAE" releases (see the repo name) — Realistic Vision's OWN model
# card says so explicitly: "For version 6.0 it is recommended to use
# with VAE (to improve generation quality and get rid of artifacts)".
# Skipping this is a real, confirmed failure: it produces a scrambled,
# striped color-noise patch over the edited region, easily mistaken for
# the separate stable-diffusion.cpp upstream masked-input bug (see
# README's other troubleshooting section) but with a different, much
# simpler cause and fix:
#
#   wget -O models/vae-ft-mse-840000-ema-pruned.safetensors \
#     "https://huggingface.co/stabilityai/sd-vae-ft-mse-original/resolve/main/vae-ft-mse-840000-ema-pruned.safetensors"
#
# Not downloading all three files is fine too — the alternative is MODEL=
# sd-v1-4.ckpt (zero setup, weakest quality) and INPAINT_MODEL left unset
# (see its own section below for why that's a real quality trap
# specifically for "remove X" jobs, not just "a bit worse" — confirmed in
# practice: a remove_target job with INPAINT_MODEL unset produced content
# with NO relation to the original photo at all, e.g. a request to remove
# an object came back with an entirely different, unrelated scene drawn
# into the masked area). See README.md "Editing and inpainting models"
# for the full explanation and an SD1.5-inpainting-only alternative that
# needs no new download at all if sd-v1-5-inpainting.ckpt is already on disk.
#
# THIS FILE SHIPS WITH THE RECOMMENDED SETUP ALREADY ACTIVE BELOW (MODEL=,
# INPAINT_MODEL=, AND YCPLT_VAE_PATH=/YCPLT_INPAINT_VAE_PATH= all point at
# the files above) on the assumption you've downloaded all three. If you
# haven't, either download them now or comment out the active lines below
# and uncomment the sd-v1-4.ckpt / unset-INPAINT_MODEL/unset-VAE fallback
# instead.
# ============================================================================

# Checkpoint filename inside YCPLT_MODELS_DIR (default "models/"). Switch
# models by changing this line only, then restart the service.
#
# Active default — File 1 from the recommended pair above:
MODEL=Realistic_Vision_V6.0_NV_B1_fp16.safetensors
#
# Zero-setup fallback (needs no download) — uncomment this line AND
# comment out the MODEL= line above if you don't have Realistic Vision:
# MODEL=sd-v1-4.ckpt

# Uncomment to override other defaults:
# YCPLT_MODELS_DIR=models
# YCPLT_MODEL_PATH=
# YCPLT_WTYPE=f16
# YCPLT_DB_PATH=data/jobs.sqlite3
# YCPLT_JOB_TTL_HOURS=24

# Optional dedicated checkpoint for masked inpainting jobs — both
# mode="inpaint" (explicit mask) and mode="img2img" with remove_target
# (CLIPSeg's automatic mask) use this slot, loaded lazily on first use —
# see conf/models.py. Leave unset to reuse MODEL for inpainting too, but
# this is a real quality trap, not just "a bit worse": a base (non-
# inpainting) checkpoint asked to repaint a wide masked region at high
# strength (which is exactly what a "remove X" job does) tends to
# produce visible color-noise/static rather than a plausible background,
# since it was never trained with the extra mask/masked-image input
# channels an inpainting-tuned checkpoint's UNet expects.
#
# Exactly ONE of the lines below should be active at a time. IMPORTANT:
# keep each INPAINT_MODEL= line on its own line with nothing else after
# the filename on that same line — a previous version of this file had a
# "<- File 2 above" note directly after the value here, which is NOT a
# comment as far as this file's value-parsing is concerned once the
# leading "#" is removed: the whole line, note included, becomes the
# literal filename, and the service then fails with "Model path does not
# exist: '...safetensors   <- File 2 above'".
#
# Active default — File 2 from the recommended pair above:
INPAINT_MODEL=Realistic_Vision_V6.0_NV_B1_inpainting_fp16.safetensors
#
# Zero-setup alternative if sd-v1-5-inpainting.ckpt is already on disk
# (see "Editing and inpainting models" in README.md) — comment out the
# active line above and uncomment this one instead:
# INPAINT_MODEL=sd-v1-5-inpainting.ckpt
#
# YCPLT_INPAINT_MODEL_PATH=
# YCPLT_INPAINT_WTYPE=f16

# VAE override — REQUIRED for the Realistic Vision "noVAE" pair active
# above (see the wget command and warning up in the RECOMMENDED MODEL
# PAIR block); most other SD1.x/SD2.x checkpoints bundle their own VAE
# and need no override (leave unset in that case). Also the setting to
# use if MODEL/INPAINT_MODEL is ever switched to an SDXL checkpoint — see
# README.md "Going further: SDXL" for that specific fp16-fix VAE file.
YCPLT_VAE_PATH=models/vae-ft-mse-840000-ema-pruned.safetensors
YCPLT_INPAINT_VAE_PATH=models/vae-ft-mse-840000-ema-pruned.safetensors

# Optional vision/captioning model (moondream2) for mode="caption" jobs —
# answering questions about an uploaded image instead of generating/editing
# one. Loaded lazily on the first caption job, not at startup. Leave unset
# if you don't need this; see README.md "Understanding an uploaded image"
# for the download links. Filenames are relative to YCPLT_MODELS_DIR,
# same convention as MODEL/INPAINT_MODEL above.
# VISION_MODEL=moondream2-text-model-f16_ct-vicuna.gguf
# VISION_MMPROJ=moondream2-mmproj-f16-20250414.gguf
# YCPLT_VISION_MODEL_PATH=
# YCPLT_VISION_MMPROJ_PATH=
# YCPLT_VISION_N_CTX=2048

# Automatic object segmentation (CLIPSeg) for mode="img2img" jobs carrying
# remove_target — see README.md "Removing a named object". Unlike every
# other model above, this one is pulled automatically from the Hugging
# Face Hub on first use (not a file you download into models/ yourself).
# CLIPSEG_MODEL=CIDAS/clipseg-rd64-refined

# Tuning for "remove X" jobs specifically (LaMa, see conf/models.py's
# get_lama_model() — this is a separate, prompt-free model from
# MODEL/INPAINT_MODEL above, requires no download setting of its own, see
# requirements.txt). Matches the code default; set explicitly here so it's
# visible without having to check conf/config.py. Raise it (e.g. 20-30) if
# a faint remnant of the removed object's edges still shows.
YCPLT_REMOVE_MASK_DILATE_PX=12

# Where LaMa's checkpoint download is cached (torch.hub) — defaults to
# models/.torch_cache, so it survives service restarts predictably and
# sits alongside every other downloaded model, rather than depending on
# $HOME being stable under systemd. Only override if you specifically
# want it elsewhere.
# YCPLT_TORCH_HOME=models/.torch_cache

# Escape hatch for remove_target jobs that also carry a reconstruct_prompt
# (see srv/worker.py's _generate_removal_edit and README.md "Describing
# what should replace the removed object"). DEFAULTS TO FALSE: four
# separate rounds of real testing, each with a different targeted fix
# (VAE, upstream stable-diffusion.cpp version, width/height alignment,
# resolution cap), never changed the actual visual defect in this SD
# masked-inpaint path, which still comes back as the same striped/
# scrambled pattern every time — see README.md "Why not StableDiffusion
# inpainting" for the full history. LaMa (the previously-confirmed-
# working default) is used unconditionally unless this is explicitly set
# to true for further investigation.
# YCPLT_RECONSTRUCT_ENABLED=false

# Longer-side cap (px) for the resolution a reconstruct_prompt job
# actually generates at. Real, reported crash: generating at a real
# phone-camera-sized upload's own native resolution pushed
# stable-diffusion.cpp's UNet compute buffer past 10GB and killed the
# worker process. 512 matches YCPLT_DEFAULT_WIDTH/HEIGHT above (this
# project's SD1.x checkpoints were trained at 512x512) — raise only if
# the machine has RAM to spare.
# YCPLT_RECONSTRUCT_MAX_DIMENSION=512

# ============================================================================
# FLUX.1 Kontext (experimental, general instruction-based editing) — see
# README.md "Instruction-based editing (FLUX.1 Kontext, experimental)" for
# the full setup walkthrough (download links/commands for all four files
# below) and the rationale (plain img2img has no way to follow an arbitrary
# described transformation, e.g. "redraw this photo as if she were a man"
# came back essentially unchanged through img2img in real testing).
#
# DEFAULTS TO OFF. This is a much heavier model (12B parameters vs SD1.x's
# ~1B) that hasn't been tested end-to-end against real hardware from this
# codebase's own development environment yet — enable deliberately, on a
# machine with RAM/disk to spare, ideally in a throwaway branch.
# YCPLT_KONTEXT_ENABLED=false

# Recommended quant: Q4_K_M (~6.9GB) — a reasonable quality/size balance
# among the K-quants. Only the diffusion transformer itself; clip_l/t5xxl/
# vae are separate downloads (see README), not bundled in the GGUF repo.
#   wget -O models/flux1-kontext-dev-Q4_K_M.gguf \
#     "https://huggingface.co/unsloth/FLUX.1-Kontext-dev-GGUF/resolve/main/flux1-kontext-dev-Q4_K_M.gguf"
# KONTEXT_DIFFUSION_MODEL=flux1-kontext-dev-Q4_K_M.gguf
# YCPLT_KONTEXT_DIFFUSION_MODEL_PATH=

#   wget -O models/clip_l.safetensors \
#     "https://huggingface.co/comfyanonymous/flux_text_encoders/resolve/main/clip_l.safetensors"
# KONTEXT_CLIP_L=clip_l.safetensors
# YCPLT_KONTEXT_CLIP_L_PATH=

#   wget -O models/t5xxl_fp8_e4m3fn.safetensors \
#     "https://huggingface.co/comfyanonymous/flux_text_encoders/resolve/main/t5xxl_fp8_e4m3fn.safetensors"
# KONTEXT_T5XXL=t5xxl_fp8_e4m3fn.safetensors
# YCPLT_KONTEXT_T5XXL_PATH=

# ae.safetensors is GATED on black-forest-labs' own repo (requires
# accepting the FLUX.1-dev license on Hugging Face and an access token) —
# see README for the exact steps and community-mirror alternatives.
# KONTEXT_VAE=ae.safetensors
# YCPLT_KONTEXT_VAE_PATH=

# Flux's guidance-distilled scale (separate from cfg_scale, which Flux
# barely uses) — 2.5 matches Black Forest Labs' own reference example.
# YCPLT_KONTEXT_GUIDANCE=2.5
# YCPLT_KONTEXT_CFG_SCALE=1.0

# Same rationale as YCPLT_RECONSTRUCT_MAX_DIMENSION above (real OOM risk
# from an uncapped generation resolution) — 1024 since Flux's native
# training resolution is higher than SD1.x's 512. Lower if RAM is tight.
# YCPLT_KONTEXT_MAX_DIMENSION=1024

# The OTHER direction of the same problem — real, reported bug: a small
# 256x198 source photo produced a Kontext "edit" that came back IDENTICAL
# to the input, regardless of prompt or quant. Confirmed to be a
# resolution problem (Kontext is trained at ~1024x1024-class resolutions;
# too small a source gives its transformer too little latent grid to
# encode any real edit) by re-testing at 2048x1536 instead, which worked
# correctly. This setting scales small source photos back UP (never past
# YCPLT_KONTEXT_MAX_DIMENSION) before generation. REAL COST, confirmed on
# this project's own CPU test hardware: ~256px took ~570s for 20 steps;
# ~1024px took ~11300s (~3.1 HOURS) for the same 20 steps — raise this
# toward 1024 only with both the hardware and the patience for
# multi-hour edits; lower it if even 768 is too slow.
# YCPLT_KONTEXT_MIN_DIMENSION=768
